question:
What is the product of the solutions to the following system of equations?
\[ \begin{cases} 
2x + 3y = 12 \\
4x - y = 5 
\end{cases}
\]

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 1 \pmod{7} \\
x \equiv 2 \pmod{11} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{13}
\end{cases}
\]
